::

Action-bar treatment (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11): Assign is icon-only (user glyph, old label as `aria-label`, verb unchanged); ✓ Mark as Done and Move to Plan KEEP their labels — both are meaning-carrying primaries per the G3 judgment rule. Ask Surfy rides the fin glyph icon-only ahead of Assign, mirroring `doc-detail.surf`'s ordering — `askSurfyTask` is the task-side grounding-chip seed (`shell.surf`, `03-tasks.surf` detail-bar ruling), reachable from real markup now that row/toolbar `action` verbs stamp `data-action` (G3).

::callout[type=note title="Renderer note — deferred"]
The live stage stepper is `::progress` (planned-20) and the 1s live tick is state-layer work (static here by design) — the markdown tables above stand in for the stepper and the Time-in-Status / Token Cost stat bands until they land. The status/priority pills ride `::badge` (also deferred) — row meta text stands in.
::

## Assign sheet

Defined ONCE in `modals/assign.surf` (`name=assign`, anchored to the Assign button): workspace member rows with the current assignee accent-checked, the Surfy Agent row (assigning to Surfy is the hand-off into agent execution, which the Token cost tile meters), and Unassigned. Opened via `openAssign` from the action bar and the Assignee tile; this file carries no inline copy.
